WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:06.901
Here's Systems as a producer. Your home screen opens on the next shoot.

2
00:00:07.151 --> 00:00:13.701
Tomorrow's canal promo: twenty-nine of thirty-two crew booked, with the three gaps listed underneath.

3
00:00:13.951 --> 00:00:21.702
The crew directory shows who's free. You see Available, Pencilled or Booked, never who they're pencilled for.

4
00:00:21.952 --> 00:00:32.903
Crew and start packs. Every rate comes from the APA card, and missing bank details, UTR or right to work are chased in one email.

5
00:00:33.153 --> 00:00:41.303
Your inbox sorts work mail into the job and drafts each reply in your Gmail. You press send.

6
00:00:41.553 --> 00:00:46.505
Permits counts back from the shoot date, council by council.

7
00:00:46.755 --> 00:00:52.506
Call sheets keep every version, show what changed, and who's opened it.

8
00:00:52.756 --> 00:01:00.507
After wrap, each timesheet arrives with the invoice made from it. Approve both, or send it back.

9
00:01:00.757 --> 00:01:10.907
When the agency asks for an extra, cost it here. They approve it in one tap, and it's added to the balance invoice.

10
00:01:11.157 --> 00:01:19.308
Rights and usage reminds you at ninety, sixty and thirty days, with the renewal quote ready to draft.

11
00:01:19.558 --> 00:01:29.709
And your cash gap puts crew money due this week next to client money due in thirty days.

